{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "006Z", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\textit{Ab}(X)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-abelian-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:048a237b0929a737c85342150af6e45c3d579f192685c5970ca0e0c01a8af6cb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d1e830b49dc4c32662ffefafd57f5eac5ac9b0ad8efebcdc2bdfa5d2a4ec2967", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> An <TEXTITOPEN_0001>abelian sheaf on <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>sheaf of abelian groups on <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis an abelian presheaf on <MATH_0004> such that the underlying presheaf of\nsets is a sheaf.\n<STRUCT_0003> The category of sheaves of abelian groups\nis denoted <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f1f1e659c5dde0279c72d2e545e5ae3ebdcf7d4e2be98dd41cb04ced99eecab", "unit_id": "tag:0070:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "006Z", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$U = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{F}(U)\n\\to \\prod\\nolimits_i \\mathcal{F}(U_i)\n\\to \\prod\\nolimits_{(i_0, i_1)} \\mathcal{F}(U_{i_0} \\cap U_{i_1})\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$(s_i)_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n(\ns_{i_0}|_{U_{i_0} \\cap U_{i_1}} -\ns_{i_1}|_{U_{i_0} \\cap U_{i_1}}\n)_{(i_0, i_1)}\n\\in \\prod\\nolimits_{(i_0, i_1)} \\mathcal{F}(U_{i_0} \\cap U_{i_1})\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4075ae4d1311027dff101f6365f6dfe9c992f7a621a524a89a9cc7ba4cef0386", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2ee15b16a867e72aa535f79ac0d83bfba9db3ea05bcf0e6713a95947b14552ac", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\nIn the case of an abelian presheaf <MATH_0002> the sheaf\ncondition with regards to an open covering <MATH_0003>\nis often expressed by saying that the complex of abelian groups\n<MATH_0004>\nis exact. The first map is the usual one, whereas the second\nmaps the element <MATH_0005> to the element\n<MATH_0006>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4ac333d337b0d5121aa1839a5fb2abbfe36d09b9f008500ddeacbda68151314", "unit_id": "tag:006Z:prose-0001"}
